# Atlas warm line — keep the existing names

Atlas owns login and the warm-line yes/no. The conferencer stays on prayphone-server. Do not merge `/agent` into the Atlas Single-Page Application (SPA) unless asked.

Words: the **agent** is the person who sits the warm line and receives calls on `/agent`. Every other participant is a **caller** (kiosk, phone app).

## Live handoff (sacred)

`src/features/atlas2026/singlepane/data-access/prayphoneSubapp.ts` calls `atlas.fn_create_prayphone_handoff` and opens `/agent#atlas_handoff=<64 hex>` (Uniform Resource Locator (URL) **fragment**, not sent to the server). `AgentAuthGate` on prayphone-server trades the code for a session and strips the hash.

## Capability

`atlas.fn_can_access_warmline_agent` returns `atlas.fn_has_permission('warmline_agent.access')`. The key is seeded on tiers `t2b`, `t3a`, `t4`, `t4plus` (`20261104190300_tier_permissions.sql`). `t4plus` also passes through `fn_is_system_admin`. Other tiers need an allow exception (`fn_admin_set_warmline_access`, `fn_supervisor_set_navigator_warmline_access`). A deny exception wins. Do not rename the Remote Procedure Call (RPC). Do not rename the permission key. Do not use Admin Directory `featurePolicy` JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) as the source of truth.

## Roles are tiers

Staff `role_key`s are the seven tiers in `tier-hierarchy.mdc` (`t1` … `t4plus`); `partner` and `enrollee` remain. The legacy JSON Web Token (JWT) claims `administrator` / `supervisor` / `navigator` normalize to `t4plus` / `t4` / `t3a` through `atlas.fn_normalize_role_key`. Do not re-add those literals as role rows and do not gate the warm line on a role literal.

## Do not

- Invent `prayphone_agent.access`
- Put JWTs in the query string
- Change kiosk camera, bridge protocol, or SignalWire join from this repo

